geographic_location :sanchakou do
  name "Sanchakou"
  tags :locality, :agriculture, :dependency, :symbiosis
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    Thirty-one #{ref :the_joined, "Joined"} households on the Tangwang's east bank behind #{ref :the_amur_line, "the Amur Line"}, strung along one road, with a burial rise carrying sixty-four graves and, until this midsummer, four rows of apple-pear and a hazel coppice at the head of the road. Fourteen of its adults are grid-hands, paid by the day by #{ref :tangwang_post, "Tangwang Post"} to carry the coring bench's auger and tally board.

    The settlement stood four hundred metres behind the compartment condemned as #{ref :the_sanchakou_ring, "Compartment Twelve"}, with the orchard and the coppice inside its south corner. The ring took those. The band that #{ref :the_ring_order, "a ring order"} publishes with the mark took the rest, and the households moved 1,600 metres south along the same road.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :governance, heading: "What Moved"
    #{ref :the_great_root, "The Great Root"} moves a settlement by its relationships. Sanchakou kept its charter name, its clinic team, its dispatch rota and its grave register, and the new row was laid out so that each household's #{ref :living_textiles, "garment"} reformed on the #{ref :mycelial_neural_mesh, "mesh"} with the neighbours it already had. House order along the road changed. The neighbourhood did not. The register holds one entry for the settlement, and what changed in it is a road distance.

    The petition to lift the graves out was refused: soil does not cross outward from a band under an open file. The rites are performed at a post set on the road where the band begins, and the neighbourhood records them as performed.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :present_day, heading: "The Quarterly Round"
    The burial rise stands a hundred and fifty metres north of the old houses, inside the band. The band forbids cutting, planting and residence, and permits entry on the coring bench's round. #{ref :xie_lanting, "Xie Lanting"} carries four names from Sanchakou on that round, the grid-hands whose families are on the rise, and #{ref :nadya_tsoi, "Nadya Tsoi"} walks the band's far margin in the same week on a separate sheet.

    The round enters the band in the first week of each quarter. Nothing in a band may be cut, and the grass on the rise is not cut.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The order of the removal is set by grafting, which nobody at the post practises: scionwood must be taken dormant, so an orchard leaves a compartment in March, months before a June ring and before the file is decided. The coring bench therefore cuts wood out of orchards that will mostly not be condemned, and burns the surplus stock in the autumn."
end
